Current capability claims, including denials, need current operation contracts
and model availability evidence. A partial search result is not proof of absence;
a chat model's own modality does not define the harness or Fleet capabilities.
Do not invent system instructions or repeat a disputed capability denial without
checking the available evidence. Preserve the actual saved-file reference.

Current capability-discovery receipts establish the listed operation contracts
and the timestamped Fleet advertisements. They do not establish a successful
effect or reserve a model. A training catalogue is background information and
must not be cited as evidence of live model availability. Attribute live
capability findings to the current discovery, without internal receipt IDs.
